  Abaddon
 The Hebrew term for “Abaddon,” avaddon, comes from the Hebrew word avad, meaning “to destroy.” Avaddon occurs six times in the OT. Closely related to death (Psa 88:10–12) and Sheol (Prov 15:11; 27:20), it is the place of destruction. While the author of Revelation uses it as the name of the angel of the bottomless pit (Rev 9:11), the OT usually presents it as a place.


