INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Faithlife Study Bible', 'Jeremias', 49, 8, 'Dedan A trading center in Arabia, southeast of Edom. The warning may be for Dedanites to avoid Edom because it will soon be judged. Judgment oracles against Edom and Dedan are juxtaposed in Isa 21:11–14. See note on Gen 10:7, and note on Ezek 27:15.

the disaster of Esau Edomites descended from Esau, Israel’s brother. See note on Gen 25:25.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Faithlife Study Bible', 'Jeremias', 49, 9, 'grape-gatherers come to you This verse is nearly identical to Obad 5. The book of Obadiah consists entirely of a judgment oracle against Edom.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Faithlife Study Bible', 'Jeremias', 49, 11, 'And your widows, let them trust in me The rest of Edom receives judgment, but Yahweh cares for the orphans and widows. See Deut 10:18; Psa 68:5.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Faithlife Study Bible', 'Jeremias', 49, 12, 'who are not condemned to drink the cup must certainly drink See Jer 25:15 and note. Yahweh did not spare His own people from His wrath, so other nations should not expect to escape. On the cup of wrath, see 25:15–26.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Faithlife Study Bible', 'Jeremias', 49, 13, 'Bozrah will become as a horror Bozrah, Edom’s capital, will experience the same fate as Judah (24:9). Compare Isa 34:6; 63:1; Amos 1:12.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Faithlife Study Bible', 'Jeremias', 49, 14, 'The poem in these three verses is essentially identical to that in Obad 1–4.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Faithlife Study Bible', 'Jeremias', 49, 14, 'a message from Yahweh The rare Hebrew word used here indicates divine revelation. It is used only here and in Obad 1.');
