INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Faithlife Study Bible', 'Malaquias', 1, 3, 'Esau I have hated The term for hate is an ancient Near Eastern covenant term. It is used here to denote rejection. Yahweh chose Jacob, not Esau, to continue the covenant relationship began with Abraham. This choice reflects a regular pattern in the OT where a younger son is favored (e.g., Abel in Gen 4, Isaac in Gen 21, Joseph in Gen 37, and David in 1 Sam 16). This recurring theme reveals that Yahweh is not bound by the conventions of human society. He is not obligated to choose someone just because of the priority of their birth.

